            <ArticleTitle>Thrombectomy for thrombus removal, filters for whatever else.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>408-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.2459/JCM.0b013e3282eee9bc</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Although effective in reducing the total embolic burden, many current thrombectomy devices might not be able to prevent the liberation of plaque components, which have been shown to be a potential contributor to the development of no-reflow during primary percutaneous coronary intervention.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
